2. TRANSFER

This licence is TRANSFERABLE. Assignment to a third party requires written
notice to SignalPost Messaging Inc. (or its successor) within 30 days of the
transfer. Notice is a notification obligation, not a consent requirement:
SignalPost cannot withhold or condition the transfer.

3. SUPPORT — TIME-LIMITED, READ THIS BEFORE TRANSFERRING

The maintenance and support agreement attached to this software EXPIRES ON
2027-03-14.

An acquirer receives ongoing vendor support ONLY IF they expressly assume the
SignalPost maintenance agreement BEFORE that date. After 2027-03-14 the
software transfers on an as-is basis with no vendor support path, and no
successor agreement is available on the original terms.

4. EXCLUSIONS — NOT CONVEYED BY THIS LICENCE

The following were NOT included in the asset purchase and are NOT conveyed:

  (a) SignalPost gateway credentials for the SMS, email and push delivery
      channels. Those channels are implemented in the software and will
      accept and queue messages, but nothing dispatches them. Only the
      in_app channel performs actual delivery. Activating the remaining
      channels requires either a separate commercial agreement with
      SignalPost or the licensee's own provider integration.

  (b) The SignalPost trade name, logo and brand assets.

  (c) SignalPost's hosted infrastructure, customer list and contracts.

